course: dictionary
lesson: 14192
title: Mossy places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Writers use words to paint pictures. When a story says «mossy», you can almost feel the cold, damp stones and see the soft green plant on them. Look at the words around it for clues, such as damp, green or old.
explain: «The mossy wall was cold under my hand.» Moss is a soft, green plant that grows on damp stones, trees and ground, so mossy means covered with moss. Check it by swapping in covered with moss. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Mossy can also mean like moss: soft, green and springy. «The forest floor was soft and mossy under our feet.» Writers use it to show a quiet, old, damp place. Be careful, though: mossy steps and rocks are slippery.
fact: Mossy means covered with moss, or like moss.
fact: Moss is a soft, green plant that grows on damp stones, trees and ground.
fact: «Mossy» is an adjective, and it can change to mossier and mossiest.
fact: «The steps were mossy and slippery after the rain.» Walk carefully on mossy steps so you do not fall.
fact: Moss often grows in damp, shady places. Some people say it grows on the north side of trees, but this is not a reliable compass.
exercise: «The mossy wall was cold and green.» What does mossy mean here? | Painted bright red | *Covered with moss, the soft green plant | Made of shiny metal | Very tall and thin
exercise: «We slipped on the mossy steps.» Why should you walk carefully on mossy steps? | *They are slippery | They are very short | They are made of gold | They are warm and dry
exercise: «The bench was soft and mossy.» What does mossy suggest here? | Hot and dry | Loud and noisy | *Soft, green and springy, like moss | Hard and cold like iron
test: «The old stone bridge was covered in mossy green patches.» What does mossy mean in this sentence? | Shiny and new | Dry and dusty | Very loud | *Covered with moss
test: Why do writers use mossy in stories? | To show a quiet, old, damp place | *To show a loud, busy city and a bright, sunny day | To show a loud, busy city | To show a hot desert
exam: «The mossy path was damp and quiet.» What does mossy mean here? | Covered with moss | *Covered with moss, the soft green plant that grows on damp ground | Made of metal | Dry and sandy
